n```\n\nThis `MyParams` type introduces two existential type parameters: one for `material` and one for `lights`. Even though `lights` is an array, it only introduces one type parameter, because we need to have a *single* concrete type for all the array elements to be able to generate specialized code."},"static":false,"obsolete":false,"line":1506,"path":"Slang/Slang/Enums.cs","anchor":"ExistentialTypeParam"},{"kind":"value","name":"ExistentialObjectParam","signature":"ExistentialObjectParam","docs":{"summary":"An existential object parameter represents a value that needs to be passed in to provide data for some interface-type shader parameter.\n\nConsider this example:\n\n```csharp\nstruct MyParams\n{\n    IMaterial material;\n    ILight lights[3];\n};\n```\n\nThis `MyParams` type introduces four existential object parameters: one for `material` and three for `lights` (one for each array element). This is consistent with the number of interface-type \"objects\" that are being passed through to the shader."},"static":false,"obsolete":false,"line":1531,"path":"Slang/Slang/Enums.cs","anchor":"ExistentialObjectParam"},{"kind":"value","name":"SubElementRegisterSpace","signature":"SubElementRegisterSpace","docs":{"summary":"The register space offset for the sub-elements that occupies register spaces."},"static":false,"obsolete":false,"line":1536,"path":"Slang/Slang/Enums.cs","anchor":"SubElementRegisterSpace"},{"kind":"value","name":"Subpass","signature":"Subpass","docs":{"summary":"The input_attachment_index subpass occupancy tracker."},"static":false,"obsolete":false,"line":1541,"path":"Slang/Slang/Enums.cs","anchor":"Subpass"},{"kind":"value","name":"MetalArgumentBufferElement","signature":"MetalArgumentBufferElement","docs":{"summary":"Metal tier-1 argument buffer element [[id]]."},"static":false,"obsolete":false,"line":1546,"path":"Slang/Slang/Enums.cs","anchor":"MetalArgumentBufferElement"},{"kind":"value","name":"MetalAttribute","signature":"MetalAttribute","docs"